#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# acsch

#% text
# `acsch(z)` gives the inverse hyperbolic cosecant.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `asinh(1/z)`.

#% item
# Exact special values and odd symmetry are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
acsch(-x)
#% output
#= -acsch(x)

#% cell
acsch(2.0)
#% output
#= 0.48121182505960347

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
acsch(0.5*im)
#% output
#= 1.3169578969248168 - 1.5707963267948966im

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(acsch(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 1.8184464592320668234836989635607090

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
